    declaration: struct-decl #45 2527:49:1-3490:67:1 name="@2::Connection" doc="An HTTP/1.1 connection that the program drives itself, as `Net::HTTP.start` gives: one request at a time, and the\nbody read piece by piece. Open it with `start`, send with `send_request`, read with `read_body` and end it with\n`finish`. The fields are the connection's own: do not read them. It belongs to the task that opened it, as a socket\ndoes, and one call at a time uses it."
      field: field-decl #30 2590:51:3-2609:52:1 name="socket" doc="The socket, a plain one or a TLS one."
        type: type-ref #29 2598:51:11-2608:51:21 name="TCP.Socket"
      field: field-decl #32 2688:53:3-2703:54:1 name="scheme" doc="`http` or `https`, the host and the port, which the request head names."
        type: type-ref #31 2696:53:11-2702:53:17 name="String"
      field: field-decl #34 2705:54:3-2718:55:1 name="host"
        type: type-ref #33 2711:54:9-2717:54:15 name="String"
      field: field-decl #36 2720:55:3-2730:56:1 name="port"
        type: type-ref #35 2726:55:9-2729:55:12 name="Int"
      field: field-decl #38 3025:59:3-3057:60:1 name="options" doc="The options it was opened with: `timeout_ms` is the time of each `send_request` (the write and the head),\n`read_timeout_ms` the time of each `read_body`, and `max_body_bytes` the largest request body. A `proxy` has no\nuser info here, so printing a connection shows no password."
        type: type-ref #37 3034:59:12-3056:59:34 name="HttpWire.ClientOptions"
      field: field-decl #41 3253:62:3-3276:63:1 name="login" doc="The `Proxy-Authorization` value of the proxy's user info (\"\" with none), alone in a channel that holds one value:\na channel prints as `<Channel>`, where a field would print the login."
        type: type-ref #40 3260:62:10-3275:62:25 name="Channel"
          arg: type-ref #39 3268:62:18-3274:62:24 name="String"
      field: field-decl #44 3462:65:3-3486:66:1 name="cell" doc="The one `Exchange` of the connection, in a channel that holds a single value: a call takes it and puts it back,\nso a second call at the same time finds it empty and says so."
        type: type-ref #43 3468:65:9-3485:65:26 name="Channel"
          arg: type-ref #42 3476:65:17-3484:65:25 name="@2::Exchange"
    declaration: struct-decl #51 3647:70:1-3846:76:1 name="@2::ResponseHead" doc="The head of a response read on a `Connection`: the `status` and `headers` (names in lowercase). The body is still\non the connection, for `read_body`."
      field: field-decl #47 3770:72:3-3782:73:1 name="status" doc="The status, however high: 404 and 500 are normal responses. An interim `1xx` head is read past."
        type: type-ref #46 3778:72:11-3781:72:14 name="Int"
      field: field-decl #50 3811:74:3-3842:75:1 name="headers" doc="The response headers."
